# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — never commit real credentials.

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Two URLs, and they are not interchangeable.
#
#   DATABASE_URL  the ops app and its API use this. In production it is
#                 Supabase's pooler on port 6543 (PgBouncer, transaction mode),
#                 which is what keeps serverless functions from exhausting the
#                 connection limit.
#
#   DIRECT_URL    migrations, Drizzle Studio and the sync worker use this.
#                 Port 5432 — a real session. pg-boss needs LISTEN/NOTIFY,
#                 which transaction pooling silently drops.
#
# Locally there is no pooler, so both point at the same embedded Postgres and
# DIRECT_URL can be left unset.

DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/slk"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/slk"

# ── Images: Cloudflare R2 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# All five, or uploading stays switched off and the Images tab says which are
# missing. R2 rather than Vercel Blob because the cost that compounds here is
# egress, not storage, and R2 charges nothing to serve an object out.
#
# Two halves that must not be confused. The key and secret write, and belong
# only on the server. The public base URL reads, is unauthenticated, and is
# what ends up in an <img src> on a storefront.
#
#   R2_ACCOUNT_ID          32 hex characters. The account, not the bucket —
#                          it is in the dashboard URL after dash.cloudflare.com/
#   R2_BUCKET              the bucket's name, exactly as created
#   R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID       from an R2 API token, Object Read & Write
#   R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY   shown once when that token is created
#   R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL     https://pub-<hash>.r2.dev, or a custom domain. No
#                          trailing slash — one is stripped anyway.
#
# The bucket also needs a CORS policy allowing PUT from wherever the app runs.
# The browser uploads straight to R2 on a signed URL, so without it every
# upload is refused before it starts. See DEPLOY.md.

# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=""
# R2_BUCKET=""
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
# R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=""

# ── Shopify ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One set per channel, prefixed with the channel's own `code` from the
# `channel` table — insert the row first, then add its three variables here.
# `slk` below is the first; add `SHOPIFY_AARTISANZ_...` the same way when that
# channel exists. A channel with no row here is one apps/sync cannot reach.
# SHOPIFY_SLK_STORE_DOMAIN=""
# SHOPIFY_SLK_ADMIN_TOKEN=""
# SHOPIFY_SLK_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
